> I have been able to get things to build, but not exactly in a suggested m=
anner.  I copied the entire target sysroot directory (~/poky/poky_build/tmp=
/sysroots/at91sam9x5ek) to the previously mentioned sysroot destination dir=
ectory.  I re-ran "bitbake meta-ide-support" just to ensure I had a clean c=
opy.  I then modified the SDKTARGETSYSROOT to point to my copied sysroot lo=
cation.  With this setup, I was able to get the project to build from Eclip=
se.  It's working, but it's a little ugly getting there.
>=20

core-image-minimal builds a very small image, which doesn't have all
headers and libraries required to link even a simple binary

> So I'm assuming I'm starting at the wrong point for the sysroot to extrac=
t.  What do other people do?=20

You have two options here:

1) Generate a standalone toolchain and sdk installer.

bitbake -c populate_sdk your_image_name

This will generate an installer script-tarball in
~/poky/poky_build/tmp/deploy/sdk/

Execute this script and follow the installation instructions. This will
extract both the toolchain and sysroot to a directory of your choice
(e.g. /opt/poky/1.6.2/).

When you configure the Yocto ADT plugin in Eclipse, select "Standalone
pre-built toolchain" before you point it to the sysroot and toolchain
directories created by the installer above.=20
=20

2) Base your image on one of the development images (e.g.
core-image-minimal-dev)

Cheers,
Todor




